{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304642-martial-arts-techniques","id":1304642,"title":"Martial Arts Techniques","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-13T10:52:48-07:00","id":1304642,"title":"Martial Arts Techniques","content":"<div align=\"center\"><u><i><b>Introduction</b></i></u></div> <br /> One of the innovations that had originally been suggested for Exalted 3e was the introduction of Martial Arts Techniques for mortal and supernatural practitioners of Martial Arts. In essence, it would give mortal practitioners a reason to purchase Martial Arts Abilities, since they could not develop Martial Arts Charms under the default rules of Exalted 3e. Unfortunately, Martial Arts Techniques did not make it to the final draft. I have decided to resurrect the concept though, and I am posting my ideas in this thread. Please tell me what you think and please feel free to develop and share your own techniques. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <u><i><b>Technique Rules</b></i></u><br /> </div> <br /> When characters purchase the Martial Artist Merit, they are not only capable of learning Martial Arts (Style) Abilities, they are also capable of learning Martial Arts (School) Specialties and Martial Arts Techniques. Martial Arts (School) Specialties cost one bonus point each during character creation or three experience points each after character creation. Characters may only develop one school for every rank in a Martial Arts (Style) Ability.<br /> Martial Arts (School) Specialties are divided into three types of schools: balanced schools, external schools, and internal schools. Balanced schools teach a mixture of decisive-only, uniform, and withering-only techniques. External schools teach uniform or withering-only techniques while internal schools teach decisive-only or uniform techniques. Unlike standard Specialties, Martial Arts (School) Specialties do not grant characters bonus dice but, instead, allow them to purchase a combination of ten Martial Arts Techniques.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts Techniques cost two bonus points each during character creation or six experience points each after character creation. Martial Arts Techniques represent permanent changes to the capabilities of characters in relation to any use of Martial Arts (Style) Abilities. Martial Arts Techniques are divided into six types: circumstantial techniques, equipment techniques, material techniques, opponent techniques, special techniques, and terrain techniques. Unless otherwise noted, characters may only purchase each Martial Arts Technique once, though the bonuses and penalties provided by Martial Arts Techniques are cumulative and universal when applicable except when otherwise noted. Characters may benefit from a maximum cumulative bonus equal to the characters' relevant Martial Arts (Style) Ability and may inflict on their opponents a maximum cumulative penalty equal to the characters' relevant Martial Arts (Style) Ability. When applicable, Charms treat the bonuses and penalties of Martial Arts Techniques as Specialties.<br /> <br /> Circumstantial techniques represent the training required for characters to take advantage of a specific circumstances while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. Equipment techniques represent the training required for characters to exploit the weaknesses inherent in a specific equipment utilization while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. Material techniques represent the training required for characters to exploit the weaknesses of opponents who depend on a magical material while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. Opponent techniques represent the training required for characters to take advantage of the predictability of certain opponents while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. Special techniques represent the training required for characters to take advantage of special situations while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. Terrain techniques represent the training required for characters to take full advantage of specific terrains while using their Martial Arts (Style) Abilities in combat. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <u><i><b>Example Techniques</b></i></u></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Circumstantial Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Amphibious Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents during an amphibious assault (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Amphibious Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls during an amphibious assault (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Solo Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents when fighting alone against a group of opponents (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Solo Offens</i>e: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls against opponents when fighting alone against a group of opponents (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Dual-Weapon Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents who use two non-cloak and non-shield weapons (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Dual-Weapon Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting opponents who use two non-cloak and non-shield weapons (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Heavy Armor Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents who use heavy armor (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Heavy Armor Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting opponents who use heavy armor (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <b>Material Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Jade Armor Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents who use armor made from jade (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <i>Jade Armor Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting opponents who use armor made from jade (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <i>Jade Weapon Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents who use weapons made from jade (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <i>Jade Weapon Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting opponents who use weapons made from jade (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <b>Opponent Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Demonic Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of demonic opponents (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Demonic Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls against demonic opponents (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Demonic</i><i> (Type) Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of a specific type of demonic opponent (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <i>Demonic (Type) Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls against a specific type of demonic opponent (Uniform).<br /> <br /> <b>Special Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Armor Training</i>: Characters gain another armor type that they may use without restriction for a single style (Uniform). <i>This technique may be purchased once per school known rather than once per character, but it only influences a single style.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Grappling Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 to the attack rolls and damage rolls of opponents attempting to grapple them (Decisive-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Grappling Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls when attempting to grapple an opponent (Decisive-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Weapon Training</i>: Characters gain another weapon type that they may use as a style weapon for as single style. Improvised weapons count as a single weapon type (Uniform). <i>This technique may be purchased once per school known rather than once per character, but it only influences a single style. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Terrain Techniques</b><br /> <br /> <i>Urban Defense</i>: Characters inflict a -1 on attack rolls and damage rolls by opponents while fighting within an urban environment (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Urban Offense</i>: Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting within within an urban environment (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Woodlands Defense:</i> Characters inflict a -1 on attack rolls and damage rolls by opponents while fighting within a woodlands environment (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).<br /> <br /> <i>Woodlands Offense:</i> Characters gain +1 on attack rolls and damage rolls while fighting within within a woodlands environment (Decisive-Only or Withering-Only).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","user":"The Fool of Creation","date":". 04-13-2019, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}